    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d44">

                <pb facs="0291" n="33" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg33"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1758</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-14T11:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1915, 11 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>273. Salandra’s ministry resigned suddenly last evening. Last Prime Minister
                    Giolitti who has majority in Chamber holds that Austria concedes or will concede
                    sufficient to obviate necessity of war with attendant sacrifices. It is rumored
                    that Sonnino, Minister for Foreign Affairs, whom Giolitti strongly opposed, was
                    more in favor of war than Salandra. Giolitti’s antiwar policy seems to dominate
                    for the present. Some excitement exists and morning paper even [suggests]
                    possibility of revolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
